<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px; color: #000000;"><s=
trong>Ronald Neil, former RNLI deputy chairman and trustee: </strong>The re=
fusal to accept two RNLI lifeboats at Southampton and Portsmouth with 120 i=
mmigrants on board has resulted, wrongly and unfairly, in the charity being=
 thrust into the political spotlight and debate. Worse still, RNLI voluntee=
rs have been threatened and abused. Whatever the arguments about immigrants=
 landing on our shores and ports refusing to accept them, the RNLI has just=
 one role and purpose. For 200 years the volunteer crews when called on hav=
e set to sea to save human life. They have saved the lives of more than 140=
,000 people. We owe it to them to recognise this and salute rather than con=
demn their actions.</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:18px">&nbsp;</p=
